Package: shaman
Type: Package
Title: Sampling Hi-C Contact Matrices for Aparametric Normalization
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Amos", "Tanay", role=c("aut")),
    person("Netta", "Mendelson Cohen", email="netta.mendelsoncohen@weizmann.ac.il",
    role=c("aut")),
    person("Aviezer", "Lifshitz", email="aviezer.lifshitz@weizmann.ac.il",
    role=c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Weizmann Institute of Science", role="cph"))
Description: Generate expected Hi-C (genome-wide chromosome conformation
  capture) data maintaining marginal coverage, and the decay in contact probability
  with increasing genomic distance. Expected Hi-C data is used for normalization
  and graphical presentation of statistical significance of observed Hi-C contact
  enrichments. The method is described in Mendelson Cohen et al. (2017)
  <doi:10.1101/187203>.
